/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 28 635 [
[(In this and subsequent patches, we'll use the [output~] abstraction to)]
[(control overall amplitude. Use the slider to control horizontally from 0)]
[(\050silence\051 to 1 \050full blast\051. Note, however, that a quartic function is)]
[(applied. In this example, you can't actually push the output amplitude)]
[(all the way up without clipping. You'll know you're clipping if, instead)]
[(of an A major chord, you hear a single, distorted tone two octaves down.)]
[(The clipping happens at Pd's last stage of audio output. Audio signals)]
[(internal to Pd have essentially no level limit.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 29 261 [
[(The output control automatically starts DSP whenever you touch the sider.)]
[(You can use the "mute" toggle to turn mute on or off.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 182 446 [
[(<-- Here we make an A major)]
[(triad as a test signal.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
